  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 8.1, the AHP decision hierarchy in the general case. A green rounded box at the top reads \"Goal: Rank m alternatives considering n criteria\". Below it a row of five blue boxes — Criterion 1, Criterion 2, Criterion 3, an ellipsis box, and Criterion n — each joined to the goal. Below those a row of four peach boxes — Alternative 1, Alternative 2, an ellipsis box, and Alternative m. Every criterion is joined to every alternative, which is the property that makes the hierarchy complete: AHP asks for a pairwise comparison of the alternatives under each criterion in turn. The edges are plain lines with no arrowheads, so the diagram asserts membership rather than direction — contrast Figure 8.3, where the ANP version is drawn with arrows.",
